{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Breeze feels like a natural follow-up to Old Sock because I want more of Clapton's relaxed blues sound.",
    "Different Shades Of Blue matches the blues guitar interest reflected in my listening to Clapton and Hendrix; the country choices also connect with part of my recent listening."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "lullaby and... The Ceaseless Roar feels too exploratory for my current wish for straightforward blues and roots music.",
    "Muddy Wolf at Red Rocks fits my blues interests, but I want a studio album today. Bear's Sonic Journal gives me too little sense of the performers to motivate a choice."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in familiar rock musicians does not mean every musical direction they explore will suit what I want today.",
    "Country and roots connections capture part of my taste, but they do not make those albums as compelling as relaxed blues on this visit."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The specific appeal of Old Sock matters: I am drawn to its relaxed blues sound, beyond simply recognizing the artist.",
    "I am choosing only a couple of albums, so a direct blues match and my preference for studio recordings matter more than a broad connection to my listening history."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understand my blues and roots interests, but spread too broadly beyond the relaxed, guitar-focused studio blues I want today."
}"}
